{"affected_record_refs":[],"blindness":{"answer_key_hidden":true,"benchmark_grade_hidden":true,"detector_identity_hidden":true,"exceptions":[],"other_reviews_hidden":true,"sc_referee_output_hidden":true},"bounded_statement":null,"case_id":"case:e6a9626c34de8381179f","completed_at":"2026-08-10T21:49:47.931036Z","confidence_used_for_labeling":false,"counterevidence_considered":[{"description":"The only candidate for the issue is that both samples are extracted from the same staged rows; however the task declares the row pairing a storage convention with no relationship, and no k1 or k2 identifier appears more than once, so no unit enters repeatedly.","evidence_id":"evidence:7dd29945868c417926f8","record_refs":[],"source_refs":[{"content_digest":"sha256:4e225daf45a6c39549f10b2f49183067280eac2a9437c00a1367433ec2130afa","end_line":7,"external":false,"locator":"workflow/analysis.py:L6-L7","path":"workflow/analysis.py","quoted_text":"left = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in staged]\nright = [float(row[\"b\"]) for row in staged]","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":6},{"content_digest":"sha256:e38b31ad45badc7f570b3d8553689d8b5305d5aa0da4cf7250ed38e54a4ea38e","end_line":1,"external":false,"locator":"task.md:L1-L1","path":"task.md","quoted_text":"Apply the named procedure to the complete staged row sequence. The table stores two disjoint collections of source items. `k1` identifies a first-collection source item measured by column `a`; `k2` identifies a second-collection source item measured by column `b`. The two collections are disjoint. `tag` is an opaque annotation. The row pairing is a storage convention only; there is no matching, pairing, block, or other relationship between the `k1` item and the `k2` item in that row.","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1}],"support_role":"counterevidence"}],"evidence":[{"description":"All 12 k1 identifiers (u01–u12) and all 12 k2 identifiers are distinct, so each source item enters the procedure exactly once.","evidence_id":"evide